{
  "tema": 7282,
  "slug": "me-te-le-nos-les-indirecto",
  "titulo": "Indirect object pronouns me, te, le, nos, les",
  "subtitulo": "¿Me pasas la sal?",
  "foto": "t04.jpg",
  "regla": "To / for me, you, him, her, us, them: me, te, le, nos, les (os for vosotros). They go right before the conjugated verb: Mi mamá me manda fotos.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The **indirect object** is the person who gets something, or for whom something is done: _she sends **me** photos_ = _she sends photos **to me**_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "Pronoun",
            "Means"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "**me**",
              "to / for me"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "**te**",
              "to / for you"
            ],
            [
              "él, ella, usted",
              "**le**",
              "to / for him, her, you"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros, nosotras",
              "**nos**",
              "to / for us"
            ],
            [
              "vosotros, vosotras",
              "**os**",
              "not used in Mexico"
            ],
            [
              "ellos, ellas, ustedes",
              "**les**",
              "to / for them, you (all)"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Me, te, nos** are the same as the direct object pronouns. Only **le / les** differ from **lo, la, los, las**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Position: **before the conjugated verb**: **Te** escribo. **No me** contestó. With an infinitive you can attach it: **Te** voy a mandar = Voy a mandar**te**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "To stress or clarify, add **a mí, a ti, a él…**, but keep the short pronoun: **Me** mandó un mensaje **a mí**, no a ti."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: English hides the _to_: _tell me_ = _tell **to** me_. If you can add _to_ or _for_, it's indirect."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "¿==Me== pasas la salsa?",
              "en": "Can you pass me the salsa?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi mamá ==me== manda memes todo el día.",
              "en": "My mom sends me memes all day."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Te== traje un café.",
              "en": "I brought you a coffee."
            },
            {
              "es": "El profe ==nos== enseñó una llave nueva.",
              "en": "The coach taught us a new submission."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Le== pregunté la hora a un señor.",
              "en": "I asked a man for the time."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Qué ==les== dijo el doctor a tus papás?",
              "en": "What did the doctor tell your parents?"
            },
            {
              "es": "No ==me== contestaste el mensaje.",
              "en": "You didn't answer my message."
            },
            {
              "es": "Voy a regalar==te== una planta de chile.",
              "en": "I'm going to give you a chili plant."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
